The markdown parser is MarkHippo's own. Two third-party libraries are shipped,
unmodified, in src/vendor/ (refreshed by `make vendor`), each loaded only when a
document needs it:

  src/vendor/temml/ — Temml 0.14.0 (https://temml.org/), LaTeX to MathML, for
  math. MIT License, (c) 2020 Ron Kok; see src/vendor/temml/LICENSE.

  src/vendor/mermaid/ — Mermaid 12.2.0 (https://mermaid.js.org/), diagrams
  from text. MIT License, (c) 2014-2022 Knut Sveidqvist; see
  src/vendor/mermaid/LICENSE.

Both licences are compatible with the GPL; their notices are kept with them.

Third-party DATA included:

  src/js/parser/entities.js — generated by scripts/make-entities.mjs from the
  WHATWG HTML Standard's named character references
  (https://html.spec.whatwg.org/entities.json), CC BY 4.0, (c) WHATWG
  (Apple, Google, Mozilla, Microsoft).

  test/fixtures/commonmark/spec.json — the CommonMark Spec 0.31.2 examples
  (https://spec.commonmark.org/0.31.2/spec.json), CC BY-SA 4.0,
  (c) John MacFarlane. Used by the test suite only; not shipped in dist/.

  test/fixtures/gfm/examples.json — examples from the GitHub Flavored Markdown
  Spec (CC BY-SA 4.0) and cmark-gfm's extension tests (BSD-2-Clause), from
  https://github.com/github/cmark-gfm, generated by
  scripts/make-gfm-fixtures.mjs. Used by the test suite only.
